WEBVTT

00:40.510 --> 00:49.270
TONIKAWA

00:40.510 --> 00:49.270
TONIKAWA

01:30.570 --> 01:32.030
Oh, wow!

01:32.030 --> 01:33.260
An open air bath!

01:33.260 --> 01:34.180
Wha... What?!

01:34.180 --> 01:36.640
What's she doing in the men's bath?!

01:36.640 --> 01:39.060
Th-This is bad! If she finds me out here,

01:39.060 --> 01:41.490
this time I'm seriously gonna be—

01:44.500 --> 01:47.520
Eek! What are you doing here?!

01:44.500 --> 01:49.500
<b>Thud!!</b>

01:44.660 --> 01:49.500
<b>What 
will 
become 
of 
their 
romance
...!?</b>

01:44.660 --> 01:49.500
<b>This week is a double feature! To be continued on page 285!</b>

01:47.520 --> 01:49.500
I should be asking you that!

01:52.250 --> 01:55.010
<i>Of course, that's how it'd 
go in a typical rom-com...</i>

01:52.800 --> 01:58.800
<b>Episode 6      Underneath the Moon</b>

01:55.010 --> 01:57.010
<i>since those characters aren't even dating.</i>

01:57.010 --> 01:59.150
<i>But we're married!</i>

01:59.150 --> 02:02.010
<i>That's way beyond just dating!</i>

02:02.010 --> 02:06.520
<b>Twin Strike Swordsman   TV Anime   Now Airing   !!

Weekly <i>Shonen 
</i>Sunday

Kamen Butler
</b>Creator: Sayama Satoru
Art: Aki Futaba

02:02.010 --> 02:06.520
<b>The new saga begins!</b>

02:02.630 --> 02:06.520
<i>The idea of the two of us visiting a hot 
spring together is both socially and legally</i>

02:06.870 --> 02:08.270
<i>completely unproblematic!</i>

02:08.790 --> 02:10.060
Here I am.

02:12.000 --> 02:15.070
Since they had it, I went and 
borrowed this cute yukata.

02:15.070 --> 02:15.780
What do you think?

02:16.130 --> 02:17.530
Uh... well...

02:17.940 --> 02:20.860
Yeah. It looks amazing on you.

02:20.860 --> 02:22.530
Really? That's great.

02:26.160 --> 02:28.160
<i>She's so cute, I'm going to die!</i>

02:28.560 --> 02:31.890
W-Well, why don't we take a look around?

02:31.890 --> 02:32.690
Sure.

02:39.170 --> 02:42.180
So this is the hot spring field, Yubatake...

02:42.180 --> 02:44.960
It's one of the things Kusatsu is famous for.

02:44.960 --> 02:49.480
That's true. But I wonder 
how long it's been here for.

02:50.430 --> 02:52.560
According to the explanation here...

02:51.690 --> 02:57.940
<b>Kyoho 11 (1726)</b>

02:52.560 --> 02:54.530
Since around year 11 of the Kyoho era.

02:54.530 --> 02:57.940
Wow. For 300 years, huh?

02:58.970 --> 03:02.950
What exactly does the Yubatake do, though?

03:03.520 --> 03:05.950
What's up with those wooden devices?

03:05.950 --> 03:07.620
They're hot water conduits.

03:07.620 --> 03:08.890
Conduits?

03:08.890 --> 03:11.630
They help cool the spring water, 
which is too hot when it surfaces,

03:11.630 --> 03:13.800
in addition to making hot spring powder.

03:13.800 --> 03:15.960
Oh, I see.

03:17.910 --> 03:18.980
Hot spring powder?

03:18.980 --> 03:22.110
You have absolutely no clue about 
things you're not interested in, huh?

03:22.840 --> 03:24.720
It's a powder that's kind of like bath salts.

03:24.720 --> 03:27.220
<b>Kusatsu
Souvenirs</b>

03:24.720 --> 03:27.220
<b>Hot Spring Powder</b>

03:24.720 --> 03:27.220
<b>Souvenirs</b>

03:24.970 --> 03:27.220
They sell it all over the place here.

03:27.220 --> 03:28.220
Huh...

03:27.220 --> 03:28.720
<b>Kusatsu Souvenir Hot Spring Powder</b>

03:28.720 --> 03:33.440
Then we should buy some for Kaname-chan 
and the others on our way back.

03:33.440 --> 03:34.620
Sounds good.

03:35.230 --> 03:43.490
<b>Hot Spring Eggs</b>

03:37.030 --> 03:40.370
Tsukasa-chan, they've got 
hot spring eggs for sale!

03:40.370 --> 03:43.490
Makes sense that they would 
in a hot springs town.

03:49.470 --> 03:51.280
Hey, darling!

03:51.280 --> 03:53.600
Since we're on our honeymoon,

03:53.600 --> 03:56.210
I thought it'd be a good idea 
to capture some memories.

03:56.210 --> 04:00.790
I don't really mind, but you 
should let me know beforehand.

04:02.340 --> 04:04.510
Come on, what did I just say?!

04:05.640 --> 04:08.510
<i>I think I'm getting better at photography.</i>

04:14.290 --> 04:19.040
I don't mind you taking pictures, but be 
careful you don't drop it and break it.

04:19.040 --> 04:20.320
Don't worry!

04:20.320 --> 04:25.280
Even if I did, I'd do whatever 
it takes to salvage the data.

04:25.280 --> 04:28.430
That sounds like something you 
could pull off, to be honest.

04:29.830 --> 04:33.160
By the way, what exactly is your 
relationship with Tokiko-san?

04:34.000 --> 04:35.420
Well...

04:37.770 --> 04:41.800
I mean, we're not related by blood, 
but she was basically my guardian.

04:42.570 --> 04:46.550
She's known me since I was little... so...

04:47.370 --> 04:50.050
She's way too attached to me!

04:50.050 --> 04:52.840
The second I let my guard down, 
she starts fretting!

04:53.940 --> 04:56.190
That's a little harsh, Tsukasa-chan.

04:57.600 --> 05:01.160
That said, I'm pretty sure she's glad.

05:02.630 --> 05:05.450
That I found such a lovely husband.

05:07.200 --> 05:11.350
W-Well, I'm glad if she's glad!

05:11.350 --> 05:13.360
And I'm sure she is.

05:14.440 --> 05:18.350
Is it me or does something 
around here smell really good?

05:18.350 --> 05:19.630
I think so.

05:21.300 --> 05:23.710
<b>O{*\3c&H627C95&}p{*\3c&H536A80&}en</b>

05:21.340 --> 05:23.710
Ramen

05:21.340 --> 05:23.710
Pottery

05:21.420 --> 05:23.710
Yakitori

05:21.850 --> 05:23.710
Look at that place.

05:24.270 --> 05:25.460
Looks appetizing.

05:25.460 --> 05:27.130
S-Sure does.

05:27.130 --> 05:30.220
There's always an itch to eat at places 
like this when you're on a trip.

05:30.220 --> 05:34.220
<b>Grilled Skewer Menu</b>

05:30.220 --> 05:34.220
<b>• Wagyu Steak Skewers</b>

05:30.220 --> 05:34.220
<b>• Pork Jowl Skewers</b>

05:30.220 --> 05:34.220
<b>• Salty Beef Tongue Skewers</b>

05:30.220 --> 05:34.220
<b>• Chicken Gizzards</b>

05:30.900 --> 05:31.650
Okay!

05:31.650 --> 05:34.220
Why don't we grab those steak skewers?

05:34.220 --> 05:38.230
<b>• Wagyu Steak Skewers</b>

05:34.890 --> 05:38.230
B-But, darling, don't you 
think that's a bit expensive?

05:38.230 --> 05:39.740
I-It's fine!

05:40.860 --> 05:43.980
I'm a wonderful husband that
you can rely on, after all.

05:48.740 --> 05:51.640
Darling, these are fantastic!

05:51.640 --> 05:53.970
Really? That's good.

05:54.400 --> 05:58.900
Come to think of it, I brought this 
thing Tokiko-san gave me, but...

05:55.520 --> 05:58.900
Special Pass

Kusatsu's Top Three Hot Springs 

<b>Goritsunoyu, Kotakinoyu, Tonokawara Open Air Baths</b>

05:59.170 --> 06:02.140
This "Tonokawara" place is 
supposed to be famous, right?

06:02.140 --> 06:05.160
Are you interested in their 
open air bath, darling?

06:06.310 --> 06:08.140
I'm not sure...

06:10.810 --> 06:12.400
Okay, here's your half.

06:12.400 --> 06:13.480
Thanks.

06:18.450 --> 06:21.340
Well, since I just used the big bath,

06:21.340 --> 06:25.150
and I want to use the open air bath in 
our room later, I guess I'll pass for now.

06:27.920 --> 06:29.910
The one... in our room, huh?

06:31.280 --> 06:32.230
I mean...

06:33.440 --> 06:35.660
Oh, look, darling!

06:41.000 --> 06:42.920
This is Tonokawara, the eastern riverbed.

06:43.700 --> 06:46.840
Wow, that's a lot of hot spring water.

06:46.840 --> 06:48.920
Kusatsu definitely earned its reputation.

06:50.580 --> 06:52.310
The ground's toasty, too.

06:52.310 --> 06:53.800
I-It sure is...

06:54.640 --> 06:59.810
<i>Even if we're married, isn't asking 
to bathe together a real challenge?!</i>

07:00.510 --> 07:02.520
The one... in our room, huh?

07:02.790 --> 07:06.370
<i>I know we're married, 
but </i>because<i> we're married,</i>

07:06.370 --> 07:08.710
<i>there are some things that 
are hard to bring up!</i>

07:09.780 --> 07:11.880
What's wrong, darling?

07:13.260 --> 07:16.910
Oh, uh, it's nothing.

07:17.170 --> 07:19.160
<i>When I calm down and think 
about it for a second...</i>

07:23.670 --> 07:27.420
<i>Is it really okay to get in 
a bath with a girl this cute?!</i>

07:30.530 --> 07:33.190
<i>It's suddenly feeling like 
a real possibility now.</i>

07:33.190 --> 07:36.380
<i>Before, it felt way too fantastical 
to be a possibility.</i>

07:36.380 --> 07:38.680
<i>Am I really allowed to go down this route?</i>

07:38.680 --> 07:42.190
<b>The Famous Tonokawara Park's
 Giant Open Air Bath</b>

07:39.980 --> 07:42.190
Looks like the open air bath is this way.

07:43.330 --> 07:45.880
And depending on the time 
of day, it's mixed bathing.

07:45.880 --> 07:46.940
<i>Mixed bathing?!</i>

07:47.240 --> 07:52.320
Well, I'd be too embarrassed to go into a 
place like that without a swimsuit, though.

07:52.860 --> 07:55.700
<i>Swimsuit? Of course! A swimsuit!</i>

07:55.700 --> 07:59.420
<i>Then again, wearing a swimsuit in 
our own private room is kind of weird.</i>

07:59.420 --> 08:01.580
<i>And besides, we didn't pack any!</i>

08:02.190 --> 08:05.720
T-Tsukasa-chan, did you want 
to visit this open air bath?

08:09.200 --> 08:10.340
Well...

08:11.110 --> 08:13.470
N-Not this one, I think.

08:15.490 --> 08:18.720
<i>I-I see. Not </i>this<i> one...</i>

08:20.000 --> 08:22.710
Th-This riverbed sure is warm.

08:22.710 --> 08:24.980
S-Sure is!

08:25.360 --> 08:27.400
Let's check somewhere else out.

08:27.400 --> 08:29.050
Sounds good to me!

08:29.480 --> 08:30.670
Ha ha!

08:29.480 --> 08:31.820
What's Important in Love

08:30.670 --> 08:31.820
Tough luck!

08:31.820 --> 08:34.990
I was actually wearing a swimsuit 
underneath the towel!

08:31.920 --> 08:33.840


08:36.800 --> 08:39.600
Did you think I was gonna go 
into a mixed bath naked?

08:39.600 --> 08:41.500
Pfft! You perv!

08:41.500 --> 08:44.290
Stupid! Don't get my hopes up!

08:41.580 --> 08:47.500
<b>Bang!!</b>

08:41.750 --> 08:47.500
<b>Sorry
 for
 getting
 your
 hopes
 up</b>

08:44.290 --> 08:45.180
Eek!

08:45.180 --> 08:47.500
The horndog's mad!

08:50.000 --> 08:52.420
<i>See, in a rom-com, it could be a coincidence,</i>

08:52.420 --> 08:56.760
<i>or maybe a trick by a third party could lead
 to them being in the bath at the same time.</i>

08:56.760 --> 08:58.840
<i>But we're married!</i>

08:58.840 --> 09:01.520
<i>It takes courage to do that 
sort of thing together!</i>

09:01.520 --> 09:04.520
<b>It's a deal</b>

09:02.070 --> 09:04.520
<i>Because you both have to agree to it!</i>

09:04.740 --> 09:07.030
<i>"Let's get in the bath together!"</i>

09:07.030 --> 09:10.520
<i>Saying those words is a 
hurdle that's so dang high!</i>

09:12.070 --> 09:14.280
<i>Can I really say it to her?</i>

09:14.280 --> 09:15.630
<i>Do I...</i>

09:17.660 --> 09:20.350
<i>Do I have the courage to say it?!</i>

09:24.020 --> 09:25.790
Now, please enjoy.

09:26.740 --> 09:31.490
I-I never knew inns had fancy 
spreads like this for dinner.

09:31.490 --> 09:34.370
We should remember to thank Kaname.

09:34.370 --> 09:35.800
We really should.

09:35.800 --> 09:38.800
Come on, let's eat while it's still fresh.

09:43.990 --> 09:45.180
This is good!

09:49.200 --> 09:50.640
You're right!

09:50.640 --> 09:52.820
Do you think it's all locally sourced?

09:53.090 --> 09:54.680
Most likely.

09:54.680 --> 09:58.760
The type of food they serve probably 
depends on what's in season, too.

09:58.760 --> 10:01.180
That means it's fresh and tastes better.

10:02.440 --> 10:05.200
That makes me want to come 
back at a different time of year.

10:05.200 --> 10:06.350
True.

10:06.350 --> 10:09.580
There are probably dishes that 
you can only get here, too.

10:10.500 --> 10:11.840
This looks good!

10:16.450 --> 10:19.060
<i>Seeing Tsukasa do things she 
doesn't get to do at home...</i>

10:19.060 --> 10:20.090
<i>Very nice!</i>

10:25.320 --> 10:26.980
What's wrong, darling?

10:28.000 --> 10:29.840
Oh, just...

10:29.840 --> 10:34.230
Being able to come to an inn like this,
 and eating a fancy dinner together...

10:34.230 --> 10:37.130
It makes for a nice change of pace, is all.

10:38.290 --> 10:42.120
I'm glad we get to enjoy 
this feast together, too.

10:42.920 --> 10:48.120
And seeing a different side of you 
from at home makes it twice as tasty.

10:48.120 --> 10:50.120
D-Does it?

10:51.880 --> 10:54.880
Dinner was delicious, wasn't it, darling?

10:54.880 --> 10:56.760
I-It sure was.

10:57.490 --> 11:01.590
There's something really nice about 
taking a relaxing trip to a hot spring.

11:01.590 --> 11:02.760
Y-Yeah...

11:03.560 --> 11:05.760
<i>Sh-Should I bring it up now?</i>

11:06.400 --> 11:09.520
<i>We ate dinner. We've had a minute to relax.</i>

11:09.520 --> 11:11.730
<i>Wh-Wh-Wh-What do I do?!</i>

11:11.730 --> 11:14.770
<i>We finished dinner, and now what comes next?!</i>

11:14.770 --> 11:18.170
<i>I mean, the obvious answer is bath time.</i>

11:19.300 --> 11:20.780
<i>B-B-But, but...</i>

11:21.530 --> 11:25.780
<i>Isn't this a moment that 
calls for manliness?!</i>

11:26.330 --> 11:29.400
<i>Asking her what we do next 
would be a dereliction of duty!</i>

11:29.400 --> 11:31.290
<i>It'd be signing off on my weakness!</i>

11:31.290 --> 11:36.110
<i>Even if she refuses, a real 
man dies facing forward!</i>

11:36.110 --> 11:37.680
<i>And so...</i>

11:37.680 --> 11:38.800
H-Hey...

11:40.440 --> 11:41.430
Let's...

11:41.970 --> 11:43.180
get in the bath together.

11:46.180 --> 11:49.400
I-I see. Impressive, darling.

11:49.400 --> 11:51.810
You came out and just said it.

11:51.810 --> 11:54.560
Right! Because I want to be manly.

11:54.560 --> 11:58.070
M-Makes sense. That's pretty rugged of you.

11:58.290 --> 12:00.540
So... what do you say?

12:05.160 --> 12:07.200
W-Well, let's see...

12:08.530 --> 12:12.080
Okay, but could you get in first?

12:18.400 --> 12:21.470
<i>Th-This is it! Me and Tsukasa-chan...</i>

12:29.510 --> 12:32.730
<i>Is this really happening?</i>

12:33.480 --> 12:38.200
<i>It feels so unreal... 
like my mind is all fluffy.</i>

12:41.740 --> 12:44.740
Is it okay if I turn the lights down some?

12:45.330 --> 12:48.240
It's too embarrassing with them on.

12:48.540 --> 12:50.870
S-Sure! No problem at all!

12:51.460 --> 12:54.400
<i>I-Is this actually reality?!</i>

12:54.400 --> 12:56.370
<i>Or is it a dream?!</i>

13:00.320 --> 13:02.380
Hey. You can't look yet.

13:04.320 --> 13:05.880
S-S-S-S-Sorry!

13:12.670 --> 13:15.830
<i>The sight of her lit by the moon</i>

13:15.830 --> 13:20.650
<i>was so radiant, I couldn't 
stand to look directly at her.</i>

13:35.880 --> 13:39.770
<i>I had no idea what to say.</i>

13:40.910 --> 13:44.670
<i>But the only thing I can say for sure 
is that this was really happening...</i>

13:45.600 --> 13:49.430
<i>And my wife is really cute.</i>

13:58.120 --> 14:01.520
Uh, well, er...

14:02.360 --> 14:04.780
The m-moon is pretty.

14:05.180 --> 14:08.280
In the Natsume Soseki sense?

14:09.550 --> 14:14.460
Oh, right, when he was translating
 the English phrase "I love you,"

14:14.460 --> 14:17.510
but thought it should be less direct
 to suit Japanese culture.

14:17.510 --> 14:18.670
If you're going to say it...

14:18.960 --> 14:21.840
I'd rather you use words that were direct.

14:21.840 --> 14:27.550
B-Because you're the only one 
allowed to say them to me.

14:32.570 --> 14:35.560
I love you, Tsukasa-chan.

14:40.040 --> 14:46.080
That reminds me of what Tokiko-san said,
about how you express that sort of sentiment.

14:47.020 --> 14:48.510
You bring that up now?!

14:48.510 --> 14:50.200
I mean...

14:50.450 --> 14:58.550
When she said it, I realized that you're 
not very direct about it yourself.

14:58.550 --> 15:00.830
That's not true.

15:01.470 --> 15:04.710
You just didn't notice before. 
I say it a fair amount.

15:06.100 --> 15:10.400
But she also said that however much 
you say it is half the normal amount.

15:10.400 --> 15:13.600
Y-You shouldn't take anything 
she says seriously!

15:13.600 --> 15:16.060
Are you not going to say it today, then?

15:17.050 --> 15:19.480
W-Well, I...

15:20.880 --> 15:22.480
Wh-What is that look for?!

15:23.560 --> 15:25.980
Fine, then! I'll say it, okay?!

15:29.020 --> 15:32.240
I l-love you, Nasa-kun.

15:35.600 --> 15:37.840
I think I'm gonna collapse...

15:37.840 --> 15:40.560
Hey! No naked collapsing!

15:42.890 --> 15:46.910
Still, hearing you say it 
like that makes me so happy,

15:46.910 --> 15:50.490
and I even love how you get embarrassed, too.

15:55.740 --> 15:56.850
H-Hey!

15:55.740 --> 15:58.600
Take that! And that!

15:57.320 --> 15:58.600
Tsukasa-chan!

16:00.770 --> 16:04.230
It felt like you were making fun of me.

16:04.730 --> 16:05.730
So I paid you back.

16:06.300 --> 16:07.500
Aw!

16:07.930 --> 16:09.230
I can do that, too!

16:10.450 --> 16:12.490
Hey! How is that fair?!

16:15.050 --> 16:20.250
<i>It's hard to put into words, but it 
felt like we both had a great time.</i>

16:20.960 --> 16:23.250
<i>And at the same time, I wondered...</i>

16:23.250 --> 16:26.750
<i>How exactly does the timing 
work for getting out of here?</i>

16:27.840 --> 16:29.700
<i>It's getting a little too hot in here,</i>

16:29.700 --> 16:32.760
<i>but between being naked and other 
issues, what am I supposed to do?</i>

16:32.760 --> 16:37.360
<i>B-But it's not like we can 
stay in here forever.</i>

16:37.360 --> 16:38.760
<i>Let's see...</i>

16:39.200 --> 16:41.750
H-Hot springs feel great, huh?

16:41.750 --> 16:43.330
S-Sure do!

16:43.330 --> 16:45.410
What a wonderful trip!

16:45.410 --> 16:48.170
<i>We were both really dizzy 
by the time we got out.</i>

16:55.260 --> 16:58.280
This is embarrassing, so don't stare, okay?

17:02.040 --> 17:05.830
<i>I remember now. Yesterday, 
we came here together,</i>

17:05.830 --> 17:08.040
<i>and then we got in the 
open air bath together.</i>

17:08.910 --> 17:10.380
<i>And then...</i>

17:10.380 --> 17:12.550
Hey. You can't look yet.

17:13.970 --> 17:15.600
<i>This is bad! Real bad!</i>

17:15.600 --> 17:18.180
<i>I'm going to die of happiness!</i>

17:18.460 --> 17:23.120
<i>Even after a good night's sleep,
 I still can't calm down!</i>

17:24.080 --> 17:28.440
<i>But Tsukasa-chan sure was cute yesterday...</i>

17:28.440 --> 17:30.460
Good morning, darling.

17:30.460 --> 17:33.000
I see your internal monologue 
is leaking again this morning.

17:33.860 --> 17:35.950
Tsukasa-chan?! Where were you?

17:36.570 --> 17:40.320
I woke up early this morning, 
so I went and used the big baths.

17:40.320 --> 17:43.280
Why don't you go, too? Breakfast 
is going to be served soon.

17:43.280 --> 17:45.960
G-Got it! I'll do that.

17:52.960 --> 17:56.290
Wow, the service here is really something.

17:56.290 --> 17:58.970
It is. Even the breakfast is very luxurious.

17:59.250 --> 18:01.350
Let's eat it before it gets cold.

18:02.180 --> 18:04.100
Okay. Thanks for the food.

18:05.730 --> 18:08.930
<i>I had the feeling my wife was being 
a little distant this morning...</i>

18:08.930 --> 18:11.110
<i>But I think I understand why.</i>

18:11.450 --> 18:16.610
<i>It's just like Tokiko-san said. 
My wife can be really shy at times.</i>

18:17.250 --> 18:22.620
<i>Which is why she has a tendency to put 
up a cool facade to hide that fact.</i>

18:22.620 --> 18:34.880
<b>He's right</b>

18:23.870 --> 18:29.130
<i>I'm so embarrassed about yesterday, 
I can barely look at him!</i>

18:29.130 --> 18:34.880
<i>He saw so much more than I'm used to, 
and my body still feels hot!</i>

18:35.300 --> 18:38.380
<i>Just thinking about it makes my 
face feel like it's on fire.</i>

18:39.460 --> 18:40.350
Tsukasa-chan?

18:41.200 --> 18:42.460
Y-Yes?!

18:42.460 --> 18:45.640
I was just thinking this breakfast was good.

18:45.640 --> 18:48.640
I-It is! It's really delicious.

18:49.040 --> 18:51.390
We've still got time before we head home,

18:51.390 --> 18:53.110
so do you want to get in the bath again?

18:53.970 --> 18:58.670
W-Well, y'know, I'm not against the idea...

18:59.160 --> 19:05.160
But doing it when it's so bright out is still... 
a little too embarrassing, I think.

19:05.160 --> 19:09.690
Oh, no, I meant that since we have 
this ticket from Tokiko-san,

19:09.690 --> 19:14.040
we could visit one of the 
baths outside of the inn.

19:14.040 --> 19:16.870
Th-Then you should've 
been specific about that!

19:16.870 --> 19:18.800
S-Sorry...

19:18.800 --> 19:20.550
I don't mind if it's bright out, though.

19:23.280 --> 19:26.060
S-Some other time, okay?

19:26.630 --> 19:28.920
<i>I found another reason to survive
 at all costs on that day.</i>

19:30.480 --> 19:33.560
Well, let's grab souvenirs for 
the others and then head home.

19:33.560 --> 19:36.980
Sounds good. We had a 
great stay at this place.

19:37.320 --> 19:41.310
Should we really leave without 
letting Tokiko-san know?

19:41.310 --> 19:44.690
It's fine. We can see her whenever in Tokyo.

19:44.690 --> 19:46.730
Really? But...

19:46.730 --> 19:49.750
Come, now. The least you 
could do is say goodbye.

19:51.700 --> 19:57.390
I'm sure you think you can see me 
whenever, but I'm a busy woman.

19:57.390 --> 20:00.020
Would a busy woman really 
be here right now?!

20:00.640 --> 20:03.410
Ever hear of the term "self-care" before?

20:03.410 --> 20:06.510
I don't even know how long I have left...

20:08.940 --> 20:10.140
Do what you want!

20:12.430 --> 20:15.440
I was wondering, are you two 
not going to have a ceremony?

20:15.440 --> 20:17.370
May as well do it up big time.

20:17.370 --> 20:19.570
Oh, right...

20:19.570 --> 20:20.900
You know damn well we won't!

20:21.170 --> 20:23.620
A wedding would be... so...

20:24.160 --> 20:25.160
embarrassing.

20:25.510 --> 20:28.410
Oh, is that right? You'd be embarrassed?

20:29.890 --> 20:33.440
Well, since we're all here, 
let's take a picture together.

20:34.170 --> 20:35.670
I don't see why we need to—

20:36.060 --> 20:37.670
Good idea. I'd love to!

20:38.070 --> 20:39.870
Darling?!

20:39.870 --> 20:43.660
Excuse me, ma'am? 
Could you take a picture of us?

20:44.890 --> 20:46.640
Okay, say cheese!

20:46.760 --> 20:48.300
<b>Aizawa Hot Springs Inn</b>

20:49.080 --> 20:51.310
Ugh, Tokiko did it again...

20:51.570 --> 20:55.800
Well, it's nice that she came to see us off.

20:55.800 --> 20:59.820
Besides, taking that picture together 
is a nice memento, don't you think?

20:59.820 --> 21:03.950
You really don't need to 
humor her so much, darling.

21:04.780 --> 21:09.760
I mean, it's our honeymoon. I'd rather
 have the memories be of just us...

21:13.180 --> 21:18.210
Th-Then why don't we make one last memory 
of this trip to Kusatsu? Just the two of us.

21:22.260 --> 21:27.370
It might be from being in the hot spring, 
but your hands are really warm, Tsukasa-chan.

21:27.370 --> 21:30.870
I-It's not because of the hot spring...

21:31.470 --> 21:34.480
It's because I get excited when you touch me.

21:36.230 --> 21:38.260
I-I see.

21:38.260 --> 21:39.000
Yeah.

21:39.500 --> 21:42.970
Okay, let's find those souvenirs.

21:42.970 --> 21:44.240
Y-Yeah.

21:44.740 --> 21:46.990
<b>Hot Springs</b>

21:47.550 --> 21:49.560
The time really flew by, huh?

21:49.560 --> 21:50.370
That it did.

21:51.000 --> 21:55.790
<i>Man, going to a hot spring 
as a couple was amazing.</i>

21:55.790 --> 21:59.250
<i>It feels like we've gotten a lot closer.</i>

22:00.000 --> 22:03.250
<i>And we've made so, so many
 great new memories.</i>

22:03.770 --> 22:04.630
Darling?

22:05.090 --> 22:08.350
You're making an interesting 
face there. Everything okay?

22:09.040 --> 22:16.080
O-Oh, I was thinking about the great time we 
had in Kusatsu, and the smile just... surfaced!

22:17.890 --> 22:21.400
Well, I had a great time, too.

22:21.990 --> 22:25.780
I'd love to go on another trip like this.

22:26.100 --> 22:27.530
G-Good idea.

22:28.100 --> 22:30.720
Maybe to Hakone or Atami next time.

22:31.460 --> 22:34.040
It doesn't have to be to a hot spring.

22:34.330 --> 22:36.780
Let's visit all kinds of places.

22:36.780 --> 22:40.040
And we'll make lots of memories together.

22:40.270 --> 22:46.290
The thought of building up those 
memories with you makes me happy.

22:46.290 --> 22:48.300
Yeah. Me, too.

22:48.780 --> 22:52.280
Will you join me in the bath again, 
even if it's not at a hot spring?

22:52.900 --> 22:54.810
Let me think...

22:55.060 --> 23:01.190
A-As long as you turn off the lights, 
I wouldn't be totally opposed to the idea.

23:01.450 --> 23:06.080
But then I won't be able to see how 
cute you are when you're embarrassed.

23:06.080 --> 23:08.760
You don't need to see that anyway.

23:08.760 --> 23:11.950
You were really cute, though.

23:16.400 --> 23:19.540
You were super cute yourself, darling.

23:24.960 --> 23:39.980
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

23:25.960 --> 23:28.090
We meet all kinds of different 
people in life, don't we?

23:28.090 --> 23:30.130
Why are you getting all lyrical on me?

23:30.130 --> 23:32.340
I'm grateful to have met 
you, too, Kaname-chan!

23:32.340 --> 23:33.970
Then how about you act like it for once?!

23:33.970 --> 23:37.720
You could start by sharing some 
embarrassing couple stuff with me!

23:37.720 --> 23:39.980
You're making all that gratitude 
I felt seem wasted!
